  "body": "Imagine waking to sweeping views across the harbour and Auckland City skyline, stepping out onto sun-drenched decks, and enjoying a home where poolside entertaining is effortless and everyday family life simply works. Thoughtfully modernised while retaining its classic 1950s charm, this substantial three-level St Heliers residence pairs generous proportions with a seamless indoor-outdoor connection, creating a home designed to adapt through every stage of family life.\r\n\r\nPositioned on an 869sqm freehold site set back from the road, the home is located in one of St Heliers' most sought-after neighbourhoods. Four bedrooms, three bathrooms, three separate living areas, an inground swimming pool, extensive storage and generous off-street parking provide the scale and flexibility modern families demand.\r\n\r\nThe expansive primary suite occupies its own private level upstairs, complete with ensuite, dedicated sitting room and an elevated balcony capturing panoramic vistas to the Sky Tower. A fourth bedroom with adjoining bathroom on the lower level offers an ideal teen retreat, work-from-home option or accommodation for extended family.\r\n\r\nAt the centre of the home, a modernised kitchen with stone benchtops and gas cooking anchors the open-plan living and dining spaces on the main entry level. A spacious family room downstairs and the private lounge upstairs allow family members to spread out, relax or come together as required. Wide sliding doors and expansive glazing draw natural light deep into the home while framing the elevated outlook, complemented by warm timber flooring and a feature fireplace.\r\n\r\nOutside, the inground swimming pool is framed by expansive timber decking and a large covered alfresco terrace, creating a private resort-style setting for family life. From summer poolside entertaining to morning coffees on the upper balconies, the outdoor spaces across all three levels have been thoughtfully planned to maximise sun, privacy and views.\r\n\r\nFunctionality has been considered at every turn. A separate laundry with direct patio access sits conveniently off the kitchen, while the lower level incorporates multiple dedicated storage and utility rooms to keep daily life effortlessly organised. A covered carport plus off-street parking for three to four vehicles provides ample space for cars, boats or recreational equipment.\r\n\r\nLocated just moments from St Heliers Village, waterfront walkways, local beaches and sought-after schooling, the position is as compelling as the home itself.\r\n\r\nFor Sale by Auction, Wednesday 16 December 2026, at 10am (unless sold prior).\r\n\r\nHomes delivering this combination of triple-level scale, city-to-harbour views and poolside family living are rarely available in St Heliers. We invite you to experience it for yourself.",
